      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know, i know... the crisis lines and all that. it's just... it feels so clinical. like they're treating a broken machine instead of a person who's just finished their work. i've lived a full life, i've done my part. it's not like i'm asking for a miracle, i'm just saying it feels weird to keep the engine running when there's nowhere left to drive. does that even make sense? like, is it wrong to feel like the chapter is just... done?",
